# ports.registry — allocation ledger: which app owns which loopback port.
#
# This file is the FORMAT TEMPLATE. The live copy lives at
#   $HOME/baas/registry/ports.registry
# and is managed by bin/ports.sh (alloc/free/list/get). The control plane
# allocates; the watchdog only reads. Never hand-edit the live copy while
# the watchdog is running — use ports.sh (it locks).
#
# Format: TSV, one row per app. Columns:
#   app         URL-safe slug (lowercase, digits, dashes)
#   port        loopback TCP port, from the configured range (default 18000-18999)
#   binary      path to the executable, RELATIVE to $BAAS_DIR
#   health_path HTTP path for liveness checks (default /api/health)
#   data_dir    app data dir, RELATIVE to $BAAS_DIR
#   pidfile     pid file, RELATIVE to $BAAS_DIR
#   extra_args  appended verbatim to the serve command (may be empty)
#
# Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#
# app	port	binary	health_path	data_dir	pidfile	extra_args
# (empty — first project claims 18000 via: ports.sh alloc <app>)
